# SRG-APP-000086-AU-000020  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to aggregate log records from
# organization-defined devices and hosts within its scope of coverage.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000086-AU-000020
group:           V-206449
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
revised:         yes
cci:             CCI-000174
control_rev5:    AU-12

contribution:    Splunk can declare the receiving input that accepts records from the
                 covered hosts and devices, a Splunk-to-Splunk receiver for forwarded data.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.

check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp] present

external:        The list of in-scope devices and hosts is organization-defined and held in
                 the site security plan; SPLK-CL-000100 directs the assessor to that
                 document to decide whether the declared inputs cover it.
external:        Each sending host's own forwarding configuration (outputs.conf on the
                 forwarder, or the device's syslog target) is configured on that host, not
                 on the instance under review.

citation:        INVENTION. The original condition named key "splunktcp" inside stanza
                 [splunktcp]. inputs.conf has no setting of that name - splunktcp is a
                 stanza, not a key - so the engine searches [splunktcp] for a key that
                 cannot exist and reports it absent on every instance, a guaranteed false
                 finding. The determined row carries an empty key, which assess.sh treats
                 as a stanza-presence test, so key is set to empty to match that
                 convention. Scope caveat for the assessor: where the covered hosts send by
                 HEC or syslog instead, the corresponding input stanza carries this
                 objective and the receiver named here would not apply.
finding:         No Splunk-to-Splunk receiving input is declared in inputs.conf, so the
                 instance has no configured means of accepting the log records forwarded
                 from the hosts and devices in its scope of coverage.
